{"tool_name":"timesets","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"timesets","home":"http://vis4sense.github.io/timesets","summary":"Temporal Sensemaking in Intelligence Analysis.","addition_date":"2021-01-18T09:21:01Z","last_update_date":"2021-02-27T09:50:34Z","biotools_curie":"biotools:timesets","edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Visualisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0337"}]}],"name":"TimeSets","owner":"zsmag19","publication":[{"doi":"10.1109/MCG.2020.2981855","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 1981-2012 IEEE.TimeSets is a temporal data visualization technique designed to reveal insights into event sets, such as all the events linked to one person or organization. In this article, we describe two TimeSets-based visual analytics tools for intelligence analysis. In the first case, TimeSets is integrated with other visual analytics tools to support open-source intelligence analysis with Twitter data, particularly the challenge of finding the right questions to ask. The second case uses TimeSets in a participatory design process with analysts that aims to meet their requirements of uncertainty analysis involving fake news. Lessons learned are potentially beneficial to other application domains.","authors":[{"name":"Biggs M."},{"name":"Nguyen P.H."},{"name":"Phillips G."},{"name":"Potel M."},{"name":"Salisu S."},{"name":"Wagstaff A."},{"name":"Walker R."},{"name":"William Wong B.L."},{"name":"Xu K."}],"date":"2020-05-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"IEEE Computer Graphics and Applications","title":"TimeSets: Temporal Sensemaking in Intelligence Analysis"},"pmid":"32356730"}],"topic":[{"term":"Imaging","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3382"},{"term":"Model organisms","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0621"},{"term":"Natural language processing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0218"}]},"bioschemas":{"name":"TimeSets","home":"https://bio.tools/timesets","summary":"Temporal Sensema